	'nt_label' => '[ Notes ]',
	'pg_ab_intro' => 'Tana Furniture was founded in 2009 by upholsterer Ines Haldane and joiner Tomas Reyes at 22 Weir Lane, Aldmoor. We build individual sofas, dining tables, and cabinetry proportioned to the real architecture of each customer\'s home.',
	'pg_ab_s1_b' => 'Ines Haldane and Tomas Reyes established Tana Furniture in 2009 after years of seeing well-made furniture fight against awkward rooms. Working from our brick premises at 22 Weir Lane in Aldmoor, Ines brought classical bench upholstery skills while Tomas brought traditional joinery and timber knowledge. Rather than manufacturing identical pieces for distant warehouses, we decided to construct furniture to order for households across our region. Over the years, our workshop has grown to include dedicated timber preparation bays and sewing benches, yet our guiding principle remains unchanged. We believe that good furniture begins with the walls, alcoves, and floorboards of the room it will occupy. Every frame is built to order, every joint is cut by hand, and every fabric cover is pulled and tacked on our workshop trestles.',
	'pg_ab_s1_h' => 'The Aldmoor workshop since 2009',
	'pg_ab_s2_b' => 'Our workshop and showroom function as a single team of seven. Ines Haldane oversees all upholstery and sofa construction, working alongside workshop lead Lukas Brandt who coordinates frame assembly and timber preparation. Tomas Reyes leads our joinery benches, cutting dining tables and cabinetry with meticulous tolerances. Mei-Lin Chou directs our textile library, sourcing wools, linens, and vegetable-tanned leathers. Amara Okoye spends her mornings and afternoons on the road, conducting our ninety-minute home measuring visits with scale ruler and tape. Clara Novak manages the Aldmoor showroom, advising visitors on timber samples and guiding orders from timber selection to dispatch. Samir Haddad leads our two-person delivery team, ensuring every finished piece is carried inside, positioned, and levelled with care.',
	'pg_ab_s2_h' => 'The makers and staff you meet',
	'pg_ab_s3_b' => 'A typical day at 22 Weir Lane begins at 08:30 when Lukas Brandt opens the workshop timber store, planes seasoned boards, and prepares mortise and tenon joints with Tomas Reyes. By 10:00, Clara Novak and Mei-Lin Chou open the front showroom doors to welcome visitors testing seat cushion depths and examining fabric books. Tuesday through Friday, Amara Okoye departs for home measuring appointments scheduled at 09:00, 11:30, and 14:30 across our 25 km radius. In the upholstery bay, Ines Haldane stretches webbing and hand-stitches wool covers until the afternoon light softens. At 16:00, Samir Haddad prepares the workshop van for dispatch, loading finished pieces ready for delivery and placement directly into living rooms and kitchens.',
	'pg_ab_s3_h' => 'A working day at 22 Weir Lane',
	'pg_co_intro' => 'Our collection comprises ten core categories of made-to-order furniture designed and built in our Aldmoor workshop. Each design is individually sized and finished to suit the dimensions and light of your room.',
	'pg_co_s1_b' => 'We organize our work across ten essential domestic categories: Sofas, Dining tables, Chairs & benches, Beds, Storage, Desks, Shelving, Rugs, Curtains, and Lighting. Unlike factory catalogue furniture produced in rigid increments, our designs serve as tested archetypes that adapt to your space. If your dining alcove requires a table slightly narrower than standard, or your loft ceiling requires a lower bed frame, we adjust the workshop drawings accordingly. We work exclusively with five sustainably sourced timbers: white oak, walnut, ash, cherry, and smoked oak. Textiles are selected for natural resilience and tactile warmth, pairing durable wool bouclé and washed linen with vegetable-tanned leather. Every piece is built to order in our workshop over an eight to ten week making period.',
	'pg_co_s1_h' => 'Ten categories built to your room dimensions',
	'pg_co_s2_b' => 'Our collection includes foundational pieces crafted for everyday domestic life. The three-seat Weir Sofa starts from £2,850, built on a solid timber frame with natural upholstery filling and tailored in your chosen fabric. The Kiln Dining Table starts from £1,980 in solid oak, cut to any length between 160 cm and 260 cm to match your dining space. The Loft Dining Chair is £395 in solid oak or walnut with a pure wool upholstered seat. For bedrooms with difficult eaves or ceiling heights, our double Ash Bed Frame is £1,450 with a sprung slatted base. We also build the Reading Desk at £1,120 and the Hall Bench at £640, each proportioned to fit tight hallways and box rooms.',
	'pg_co_s2_h' => 'Core workshop pieces and prices',
	'pg_ct_intro' => 'Whether you want to discuss a custom dining table length, check fabric samples, or book a measuring appointment, we welcome your enquiries by email, phone, or in person.',
	'pg_ct_s1_b' => 'You can reach our Aldmoor workshop directly by telephone on +44 1632 960 214 or by sending an email to hello@tanafurniture.example. Our team reviews all incoming enquiries daily and replies promptly with specific advice. If you prefer to visit our showroom and workshop in person, our address is 22 Weir Lane, Aldmoor. We are open Tuesday through Saturday from 10:00 to 18:00 and Sunday from 11:00 to 16:00. We are closed on Mondays when our makers concentrate on timber cutting and frame assembly.',
	'pg_ct_s1_h' => 'How can I get in touch with the workshop?',
	'pg_ct_s2_b' => 'When writing to us about a potential commission or home visit, it is helpful to provide a few practical details. Tell us which furniture piece you are considering—such as the Weir Sofa, Kiln Dining Table, or Ash Bed Frame—along with your approximate room dimensions and your home postcode. If you have specific timber preferences like white oak or walnut, or upholstery questions regarding wool or linen, mention them in your message. Clara Novak or Amara Okoye will reply to confirm options, lead times, or appointment slots.',
	'pg_ct_s2_h' => 'What details should I provide about my project?',
	'pg_dl_intro' => 'We believe delivery is the final stage of craftsmanship, not a task to hand over to external parcel couriers. Our own two-person workshop team brings your furniture into your home and places it ready for use.',
	'pg_dl_s1_b' => 'Every delivery is managed by our dedicated delivery and placement lead, Samir Haddad, accompanied by an experienced workshop colleague. Because our team understands how the joinery and upholstery were constructed, they handle your furniture with exceptional care. We carry pieces through narrow doorways, navigate awkward stair turns, and bring items directly into your designated room. Once inside, our crew assembles bed frames, attaches table legs, adjusts levelling glides for uneven timber floorboards, and checks cushion alignment. We remove all protective blankets and packaging materials, carrying them back to the workshop so your room is clean and ready to live in.',
	'pg_dl_s1_h' => 'Careful placement by our workshop team',
	'pg_dl_s2_b' => 'We provide delivery and placement within a 40 km radius of our Aldmoor workshop for a fixed fee of £85. For addresses beyond 40 km, Clara Novak prepares an individual delivery quote based on distance and access requirements. To simplify your room transition, we also offer an old piece removal service for £30 per item when delivering your new furniture. Rather than sending unwanted furniture to commercial landfill, Samir and his team ensure all collected pieces are either donated to local community reuse initiatives or cleanly recycled in the Aldmoor area.',
	'pg_dl_s2_h' => 'Delivery zones, transparent fees, and old piece removal',
	'pg_jr_intro' => 'Our journal records honest reflections on furniture making, room proportions, timber selection, and the physical realities of delivering handmade pieces into everyday homes.',
	'pg_jr_s1_b' => 'The Tana Furniture journal is written directly by our makers and measuring team in Aldmoor. Rather than offering generic decorating trends, our articles document the practical craft of bespoke furniture. We explain how joinery responds to indoor central heating, how cushion fillings soften over time, and how room layout choices affect daily comfort. We also detail the challenges of fitting large solid wood furniture into older houses with narrow doors, tight corridors, and unlevel floors, sharing solutions drawn from fifteen years of workshop experience.',
	'pg_jr_s1_h' => 'What topics do our journal notes explore?',
	'pg_jr_s2_b' => 'Our recent essays span every stage of our four-part process. In \'How we measure a room in ninety minutes\', Amara Okoye explains how our home visits capture room architecture and domestic habits. In \'Inside the workshop: a sofa frame, week three\', Lukas Brandt and Ines Haldane document the jointing, springing, and upholstery of a bespoke Weir Sofa. In \'Getting a sideboard up a narrow stair\', delivery lead Samir Haddad shares techniques for navigating tight turns and historic townhouses across our 40 km delivery area.',
	'pg_jr_s2_h' => 'Which workshop essays can you read here?',
	'pg_me_intro' => 'A successful piece of furniture must navigate narrow stairwells, sit flush against uneven plaster, and leave room for everyday domestic routines. Our home measuring visit assesses your space before any wood is cut.',
	'pg_me_s1_b' => 'During a home visit, Amara Okoye evaluates four distinct physical conditions. First, she measures walls and alcoves, noting skirting depths, socket placements, and chimney breast projections. Second, she inspects access routes including doorways, tight staircases, and turning landings to ensure finished pieces can enter safely. Third, she observes natural daylight and window placement, checking how sunlight falls across seating areas and timber surfaces throughout the day. Finally, she notes how your household sits, eats, and moves through the room, ensuring that dining chairs pull back without scraping walls and coffee tables leave clear walkways. These four factors determine the final proportions of your custom furniture.',
	'pg_me_s1_h' => 'Four essential aspects of our room assessment',
	'pg_me_s2_b' => 'Home measuring visits take place Tuesday to Friday with three daily slots: 09:00, 11:30, and 14:30. The visit lasts about 90 minutes and costs £45 within our 25 km radius of Aldmoor, a fee fully deducted from any furniture order over £1,000. Before the visit, Clara Novak discusses your requirements by phone or email. During the ninety minutes, Amara measures your room with steel tapes and scale rulers while presenting timber samples and fabric swatches in your room\'s natural light. Afterwards, Amara returns to the workshop to draw up precise dimensioned sketches and specifications for Ines and Tomas to review before cutting timber.',
	'pg_me_s2_h' => 'Before, during, and after the ninety-minute visit',
	'pg_mo_intro' => 'We do not hold finished stock in commercial warehouses or ship flat-packed boxes. Every sofa, dining table, and cabinet is made to order on our benches in Aldmoor over eight to ten weeks.',
	'pg_mo_s1_b' => 'The life of each piece begins on the joinery bench with Tomas Reyes and Lukas Brandt. We select five distinct woods in daylight: white oak, walnut, ash, cherry, and smoked oak, allowing natural grain variations and character to show through under clear linseed oil. For upholstered pieces like the Weir Sofa, starting from £2,850, we build heavy solid wood frames engineered to endure decades of continuous domestic use. For tables like the Kiln Dining Table, starting from £1,980, we cut solid oak planks to your exact room length between 160 cm and 260 cm. Every joint is machined and hand-fitted in our Aldmoor workshop, ensuring structural permanence without decorative excess.',
	'pg_mo_s1_h' => 'Frames, joinery, and timber species',
	'pg_mo_s2_b' => 'Once the wooden frame is assembled, Ines Haldane and Mei-Lin Chou oversee the upholstery and finishing stages. Mei-Lin guides you through our swatch books, comparing wool bouclé, washed linen, wool felt, and supple vegetable-tanned leather against your room\'s natural daylight. Ines stretches jute webbing, ties coil springs, and layers natural wool felt before pulling and stitching your chosen cloth. The making process takes between eight and ten weeks from the confirmation of workshop drawings. We require a 30% deposit to secure workshop bench time and purchase materials, with the remaining balance settled upon delivery and placement in your home.',
	'pg_mo_s2_h' => 'Fabrics, hand upholstery, and workshop finishes',
	'pg_nl_intro' => 'Subscribe to receive our quiet seasonal letter sent directly from 22 Weir Lane in Aldmoor. We write four times a year with timber notes, workshop updates, and finished room stories.',
	'pg_nl_s1_b' => 'We publish exactly one letter per season—in spring, summer, autumn, and winter. In each edition, Ines Haldane and Tomas Reyes share genuine updates from our Aldmoor benches. We discuss newly arrived timber batches such as white oak, walnut, and ash, explain the joinery techniques behind recent bespoke orders, and announce new fabric swatch additions from Mei-Lin Chou. We also include photographic field notes from recent room installations completed by Samir Haddad and Amara Okoye, offering practical design insights for domestic interiors.',
	'pg_nl_s1_h' => 'What will you receive in our seasonal letter?',
	'pg_nl_s2_b' => 'We respect your inbox and treat your personal contact details with the same care we apply to our furniture. We send only our four seasonal newsletters and will never bombard you with weekly promotional messages, artificial sales events, or third-party marketing. We make no other use of your email address beyond delivering these letters. Every email includes a clear, immediate unsubscribe link should you ever decide to stop receiving them, or you can email hello@tanafurniture.example at any time to remove your details.',
	'pg_nl_s2_h' => 'How do you handle subscriber privacy and email data?',
	'pg_pr_intro' => 'We maintain open, transparent pricing for all our workshop furniture and home services. Every price reflects honest materials, bench craftsmanship, and realistic delivery care without hidden surcharges.',
	'pg_pr_s1_b' => 'Our prices are fixed and straightforward. A home measuring visit within 25 km is £45 for a ninety-minute appointment, which is deducted from any order over £1,000. The three-seat Weir Sofa starts from £2,850 made to order in your chosen fabric over eight to ten weeks. The Kiln Dining Table in solid oak is from £1,980, cut to length between 160 cm and 260 cm. The Loft Dining Chair in oak or walnut with a wool seat is £395. The double Ash Bed Frame with a slatted base made to your ceiling height is £1,450. Delivery and placement by our two-person team within 40 km is £85. Having your old piece taken away for local reuse or recycling is £30.',
	'pg_pr_s1_h' => 'What are your standard furniture prices and workshop rates?',
	'pg_pr_s2_b' => 'All prices listed on our price schedule include VAT at standard rates. When you commission a made-to-order piece from Tana Furniture, we ask for a 30% deposit upon approval of workshop drawings and fabric selection. This deposit allows Tomas Reyes and Lukas Brandt to select your timber and reserves production time on our joinery and upholstery benches. The remaining 70% balance is payable only after your furniture has been delivered, placed, and inspected by Samir Haddad in your home. We accept payment by bank transfer or debit card, and our quotes remain valid for thirty days.',
	'pg_pr_s2_h' => 'How do payment terms, deposits, and VAT work?',
	'pg_rm_intro' => 'Rather than designing furniture for abstract showrooms, we fit each piece to the awkward angles, low eaves, and tight corners of real homes. Here are three domestic case studies from our workshop.',
	'pg_rm_s1_b' => 'In a converted attic bedroom with eaves dropping to just 1.9 m, a local couple struggled to position a standard bed without blocking natural light or wasting awkward floor space. Tomas Reyes designed a custom double Ash Bed Frame (£1,450) with headboard posts trimmed lower to fit snugly beneath the roof slope. Beneath the slatted mattress base, the workshop integrated deep pull-out storage drawers calibrated to the exact pitch of the eaves. The pale English ash grain brightened the shadowed ceiling line, turning a previously unusable roof space into a calm and functional sleeping loft.',
	'pg_rm_s1_h' => 'A bed under a sloping roof',
	'pg_rm_s2_b' => 'A spare box room measuring just 2.1 × 2.4 m presented a challenging work-from-home problem for a household in Aldmoor. A large cast-iron radiator beneath the window occupied valuable wall length. Lukas Brandt and Tomas Reyes built our Reading Desk (£1,120) with custom leg spacing that spanned the radiator pipework without blocking heat circulation. Above the desk, we installed slim solid oak wall shelving scribed directly into the plaster alcove. By utilizing the room\'s vertical height and accounting for the heating fixtures, the small box room was transformed into a productive, uncluttered study.',
	'pg_rm_s2_h' => 'A study in the box room',
	'pg_rm_s3_b' => 'A family of five needed daily dining seating in a compact kitchen corner without obstructing the walkway to the garden terrace. Standard dining sets either overcrowded the room or blocked doorway access. We crafted a Kiln Dining Table in solid oak, cut specifically to a 190 cm length, and paired it with a matching Hall Bench (£640) tucked flush against the perimeter wall. Two Loft Dining Chairs (£395 each) sat opposite. This arrangement seated all five family members and a guest comfortably while keeping traffic paths entirely clear.',
	'pg_rm_s3_h' => 'Six at a kitchen corner',
	'pg_vi_intro' => 'Our Aldmoor showroom is situated at 22 Weir Lane, right in front of our working joinery and upholstery benches. We encourage you to visit, sit on our sofas, examine wood finishes, and talk through your room plans.',
	'pg_vi_s1_b' => 'The Tana Furniture showroom is located at 22 Weir Lane, Aldmoor. We are open Tuesday to Saturday from 10:00 to 18:00, and Sunday from 11:00 to 16:00; we are closed on Mondays. If you travel by rail, our workshop is an easy 6-minute walk from Aldmoor railway station. If you arrive by car, we provide dedicated off-street parking for 4 cars in our front yard. Clara Novak is on hand throughout the week to guide you through timber samples, leather hides, and upholstery fabrics, or to answer questions about workshop availability.',
	'pg_vi_s1_h' => 'Where is the showroom and when are you open?',
	'pg_vi_s2_b' => 'To arrange a ninety-minute home measuring visit with Amara Okoye, contact us by email at hello@tanafurniture.example, telephone +44 1632 960 214, or use our booking form. Measuring appointments are available Tuesday to Friday with slots at 09:00, 11:30, and 14:30 within our 25 km service radius. Please let us know your preferred day and time slot, your home postcode, and the specific room you wish to furnish. The £45 visit fee is credited against any subsequent furniture order over £1,000.',
	'pg_vi_s2_h' => 'How do I book a home measuring visit?',
